From 6c4e30d358a3a10aa01ae9b40ec0824255c88a7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Hotchkiss <chris@hotchkiss.io>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 18:22:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] P3: return ENETUNREACH (not EADDRNOTAVAIL) for offline
 public-IP connects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When networking is "Disconnected" (RPCS3 Net: Internet enabled: Disconnected,
i.e. get_net_status() is false), lv2_socket_native::connect() to a public IP
returns an error to the guest. Upstream returns SYS_NET_EADDRNOTAVAIL ("can't
assign requested address"), which some titles — notably Skylanders: Spyro's
Adventure — treat as a transient, retryable glitch: they busy-respawn
download-worker threads forever, pinning every CPU core and starving the
RSX/render thread until the controller's 8s freeze-watchdog restarts the
emulator (HTPC repro 2026-05-30).

A physically unplugged adapter returns SYS_NET_ENETUNREACH ("network is
unreachable"), which games treat as permanent -> they disable online and play
offline cleanly. Returning ENETUNREACH on this path makes "Disconnected" look
like a yanked cable, which is the behaviour offline play actually wants.

Inert under the controller's shipped config (Internet enabled: Connected + PSN
Disconnected — the one stable mode, where connects succeed so this branch isn't
taken), but a genuine fix for the offline path. Independent of P1/P2 (touches
Emu/Cell/lv2/sys_net, not the portal device or the game window).

Tested via the controller's live freeze-repro; no automated C++ test added —
this is emulator-side net behaviour gated on a real game's retry policy, so a
unit test would only re-assert the constant. See rpcs3-patches/README.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rpcs3/Emu/Cell/lv2/sys_net/lv2_socket_native.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rpcs3/Emu/Cell/lv2/sys_net/lv2_socket_native.cpp b/rpcs3/Emu/Cell/lv2/sys_net/lv2_socket_native.cpp
index b422db814..dbe0ac43b 100644
--- a/rpcs3/Emu/Cell/lv2/sys_net/lv2_socket_native.cpp
+++ b/rpcs3/Emu/Cell/lv2/sys_net/lv2_socket_native.cpp
@@ -224,7 +224,16 @@ std::optional<s32> lv2_socket_native::connect(const sys_net_sockaddr& addr)
 	auto& nph = g_fxo->get<named_thread<np::np_handler>>();
 	if (!nph.get_net_status() && is_ip_public_address(native_addr))
 	{
-		return -SYS_NET_EADDRNOTAVAIL;
+		// P3 (Skylander controller, PLAN 16.x): when networking is "Disconnected",
+		// a public-IP connect should look like a YANKED CABLE, not a transient
+		// source-address glitch. Upstream returns EADDRNOTAVAIL ("can't assign
+		// requested address"), which some titles (Skylanders: Spyro's Adventure)
+		// classify as retryable -> they busy-respawn download-worker threads
+		// forever, pinning every core and starving the RSX/render thread until the
+		// 8s freeze-watchdog restarts the emulator (HTPC repro 2026-05-30). A real
+		// unplugged adapter returns ENETUNREACH ("network is unreachable"), which
+		// games treat as permanent -> they disable online and play offline cleanly.
+		return -SYS_NET_ENETUNREACH;
 	}
 
 	if (psa_in->sin_port == 53)
-- 
